{0 Hedgehog}

{i Property-based testing with integrated shrinking for OCaml.}

Hedgehog is a property-based testing library in the spirit of
{{:https://hedgehog.qa}Haskell Hedgehog}. It provides:

- {b Integrated shrinking} — generators produce a rose tree of outcomes,
  so every generator shrinks for free. No manual shrink functions needed.
- {b Range-controlled generation} — numeric ranges separate the concept
  of bounds from the origin, giving you precise control over value
  distribution and shrink direction.
- {b Algebraic effects for assertions} — test bodies use OCaml 5
  effects for [assert_], [annotate], [cover], and more, keeping
  generator and test logic cleanly separated.
- {b State machine testing} — the {!Hedgehog.Stm} module lets you test
  stateful systems against abstract models, with sequential and
  parallel linearizability checking.

{1 Quick example}

{@ocaml[
  open Hedgehog

  let () =
    Property.check
      Property.(property Gen.(
        let* xs = list (Range.linear 0 100) (int (Range.linear 0 1000)) in
        return (fun () ->
          assert_ (List.rev (List.rev xs) = xs))))
    |> ignore
]}

